placedFrom.description:
How the order was placed: `quote` (a held quote) or `stream` (a Live prices row);
`unrecorded` for a trade placed before this was recorded or outside `POST /orders`,
never to be read as a quote order. The order read's `operation.placedFrom`. Treat the set as open.

data.description:
Bytes passed to the receiving contract or program with the delivery, hex-encoded;
networks that take none refuse it. Today no venue delivers with it: each refuses the
request per source with reason `deliverToCalldataUnsupported`.

unreachable.description:
Empty when this read reached the LP's movement history. Otherwise one entry: source
`lpHistory`, reason the observation's reasonCode, readAt its last successful read if any;
the recorded movements are still listed.

validFor.description:
Whole seconds, at `computedAt`, that this row's `priceId`s may still be ordered against;
absent when the row is not tradable. Each `priceId` carries its own expiry, which is what an
order is judged by.

product.description:
The protocol product this leg runs (`cctp`, `acrossBridge`, …), from the served route;
absent on a venue-account leg or when the route does not name it. Never parsed out of
`venue.name`, which is display text.

QuoteNextActionSign.description:
Only on an order: sign `step` and submit it to `POST /api/v1/orders/{orderId}/steps/{stepId}`
before its `signBy`. The order's source wallet is one the client signs for itself;
nothing is sent until the step is submitted.

